{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula","title":"prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.md","line":451,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex#prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-divergence-lie-derivative]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-dual-one-form]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex","label":"prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula","line":926,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[Divergence as adjoint of $\\theta_X$]\n  \\label{prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0077}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint, def:pet-ch2-divergence-lie-derivative, def:pet-ch2-dual-one-form}\n\n  \\dcref{ch2:2.2.7}\n  If $X$ is a vector field with dual $1$-form $\\theta_X$, then\n  $\\operatorname{div}X=-\\nabla^*\\theta_X$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula}\n\n  \\sketch\n  In an orthonormal frame,\n  \\[\n    -\\nabla^*\\theta_X\n      =\\sum_i(\\nabla_{E_i}\\theta_X)(E_i)\n      =\\sum_i g(\\nabla_{E_i}X,E_i)\n      =\\sum_i\\tfrac12(L_Xg)(E_i,E_i).\n  \\]\n  The final sum is $\\operatorname{div}X$ by\n  \\cref{prop:pet-ch2-divergence-trace-formula}.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[Divergence as adjoint of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\theta _X$\">$\\theta _X$</span>] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a7065742d6368322d646976657267656e63652d61646a6f696e742d666f726d756c61\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0077</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23def%3Apet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint\">↗ def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23def%3Apet-ch2-divergence-lie-derivative\">↗ def:pet-ch2-divergence-lie-derivative</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23def%3Apet-ch2-dual-one-form\">↗ def:pet-ch2-dual-one-form</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.2.7</span></span>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$X$\">$X$</span> is a vector field with dual <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1$\">$1$</span>-form <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\theta _X$\">$\\theta _X$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {div}X=-\\nabla ^*\\theta _X$\">$\\operatorname {div}X=-\\nabla ^*\\theta _X$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23prop%3Apet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula\">↗ prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula</a> </p><p>\\sketch In an orthonormal frame, </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  -\\nabla ^*\\theta _X =\\sum _i(\\nabla _{E_i}\\theta _X)(E_i) =\\sum _i g(\\nabla _{E_i}X,E_i) =\\sum _i\\tfrac 12(L_Xg)(E_i,E_i).  \\]\">\\[  -\\nabla ^*\\theta _X =\\sum _i(\\nabla _{E_i}\\theta _X)(E_i) =\\sum _i g(\\nabla _{E_i}X,E_i) =\\sum _i\\tfrac 12(L_Xg)(E_i,E_i).  \\]</span></p><p> The final sum is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {div}X$\">$\\operatorname {div}X$</span> by <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23prop%3Apet-ch2-divergence-trace-formula\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-divergence-trace-formula\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a7065742d6368322d646976657267656e63652d74726163652d666f726d756c61\">subsection 1.3</a>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-adjoint-integral-identity","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint","title":"def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint","label":"def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-divergence-lie-derivative","title":"def:pet-ch2-divergence-lie-derivative","label":"def:pet-ch2-divergence-lie-derivative"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-dual-one-form","title":"def:pet-ch2-dual-one-form","label":"def:pet-ch2-dual-one-form"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula","title":"prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula","label":"prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula","title":"prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula","label":"prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula","title":"prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[Divergence as adjoint of $\\theta_X$]\n  \\label{prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0077}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint, def:pet-ch2-divergence-lie-derivative, def:pet-ch2-dual-one-form}\n\n  \\dcref{ch2:2.2.7}\n  If $X$ is a vector field with dual $1$-form $\\theta_X$, then\n  $\\operatorname{div}X=-\\nabla^*\\theta_X$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula}\n\n  \\sketch\n  In an orthonormal frame,\n  \\[\n    -\\nabla^*\\theta_X\n      =\\sum_i(\\nabla_{E_i}\\theta_X)(E_i)\n      =\\sum_i g(\\nabla_{E_i}X,E_i)\n      =\\sum_i\\tfrac12(L_Xg)(E_i,E_i).\n  \\]\n  The final sum is $\\operatorname{div}X$ by\n  \\cref{prop:pet-ch2-divergence-trace-formula}.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint","title":"def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-divergence-lie-derivative","title":"def:pet-ch2-divergence-lie-derivative","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-dual-one-form","title":"def:pet-ch2-dual-one-form","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}